session:pr593Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #509 asked for the W3C OWL 2 Mapping to RDF Graphs blank-node structural encoding for complex (non-atomic) class expressions in owl2rl2datalog::owl_to_rdf -- owl:unionOf/intersectionOf/complementOf/oneOf over rdf:List, and owl:Restriction nodes for the existential/universal/hasValue/hasSelf/cardinality forms -- since Translator::named_class previously returned None for anything but a ClassName or AnonymousClass, causing every axiom mentioning one to be recorded in RdfTranslationReport::skipped rather than translated (established by earlier PR #370, which deliberately deferred this general machinery). The exact triple shapes were fetched live from the spec's Table 1 rather than assumed, confirming e.g. that DataSomeValuesFrom/DataAllValuesFrom use owl:onProperty for a single data property but owl:onProperties over an rdf:List for two or more, and that qualified cardinalities carry owl:onClass (object) or owl:onDataRange (data) alongside the xsd:nonNegativeInteger-typed cardinality literal. The key design decision was making the new Translator::class_expression method return Option<GraphElementId> rather than infallible, even though every complex ClassExpression variant can in principle be encoded: a restriction's own ObjectPropertyExpression can still be an unsupported InverseObjectProperty/ObjectPropertyChain (issue #510) and a restriction's DataRange can still be a complex one requiring #512's still-unbuilt encoding, so keeping it Option and propagating None via '?' before minting any blank node for the enclosing expression avoids ever leaving a partially-formed/orphaned blank node in the datastore when a nested part turns out to be unsupported -- named_class's existing Option convention was reused rather than invented fresh. class_expression recurses into itself for nested ClassExpression operands, verified by a SubClassOf(A, ObjectUnionOf(B, ObjectIntersectionOf(C, D))) test walking the resulting rdf:List cells down two levels. Four previously-passing 'must be skipped' tests (for SubClassOf, ClassAssertion, DisjointUnion, and HasKey on a complex class expression) were flipped to positive assertions now that these axioms translate instead of skip, rather than being left stale alongside new tests that would have duplicated their coverage." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:593 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr593 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
